0 HYBRID HYBRIDS ASCENSION RESPEC~
Hybrid conversion, pure-class ascension and path respec are not enabled.
HYBRID and HYBRID <parent> are read-only development previews.
There are 19 planned parents and 171 distinct two-parent combinations.
The intended design gives hybrids both parent kits; pure-class ascension
is a separate balancing path. Previewing cannot convert or spend resources.
~

0 HYBRIDROSTER HYBRIDNAMES~
The named Genesis Reforged roster contains all 171 distinct two-parent pairs
from the 19 standalone classes. Parent order does not change the identity.
Use hybrid roster to list every name, or hybrid roster <parent> for its 18
combinations. Use hybrid pair <first parent> <second parent> for one pair.
Examples: hybrid pair vampire werewolf shows Bloodfang;
hybrid pair angel demon shows Nephilim.
These commands are READ-ONLY previews. They cannot enroll a hybrid, grant
inherited powers, spend resources, alter saves or change your existing class.
Class Leader exclusion is a required future rule, not an active conversion.
Pure-class ascension remains separate and unavailable.
~

0 KITSTATUS~
All 19 standalone class identities have gameplay code. Defined Genesis
catalogues include Angel 33, Demon 71 and Cyborg 60 implemented entries.
New native kits and restored abilities
have dedicated effect, safety, persistence and sanitizer regressions.
This does NOT certify every legacy skill argument, every upstream variant,
all multiplayer balance, or playable hybrids. Broader legacy verification
is ongoing; developer coverage records explicitly retain unverified cases.
Use each class's live menu and HELP KITS for current gameplay instructions.
~

0 BOOKWRITING WRITESPELL~
Hold/read your primer and read its fifth page for a tested writing recipe.
To make another Spark, remove the held book and hold the inscription pen:
  remove primer
  sorccreate page
  hold pen
  write page title My Spark
  write page line start.damage.spell
  write page line message.1: sparks
  write page line message.2: You send sparks toward $N.
  write page line message.3: $n sends sparks toward $N.
  write page line end.yellow
  remove pen
  cast 'insert page' page primer
  hold primer
  turn primer 6
  chant <enemy>
Six assumes the original five-page primer. Use its index to find later pages.
For a protective armor spell use start.affect.spell, apply: armor,
duration: 2, the three messages, and end.green. Do not use reversed:
Genesis armor is positive for defense. Crafting and casting costs still apply.
~

7 RELEVEL~
Owner bootstrap: only the exact player name Admin (case-insensitive) may
self-relevel to the highest rank, level 7. Prior name lists were removed.
NPCs and switched descriptors cannot use the bootstrap.
Secure the Admin account before public registration. This command does not
reserve/create the account or demote existing staff. Save normally afterward.
~

0 KNOWALIGNMENT KNOW_ALIGNMENT~
Know Alignment reads a visible NPC in your current room. It reports the
NPC's area-defined alignment number and whether it is good, neutral or evil.
It does not assign alignment to players or read distant/hidden targets.
The spell name is 'know alignment'; access depends on normal spell or item
requirements.
~

0 FRENZY FRENZYSPELL~
Frenzy grants a named, timed battle-rage effect: +1 hitroll and +1 damroll.
It does not force combat or toggle a Vampire/Werewolf class-rage state.
Repeated applications do not stack. Expiry/removal restores the old values.
The spell name is frenzy; normal spell or item requirements still apply.
~

0 DARKBLESSING DARKBLESS~
Darkblessing supports evil NPCs only: their area alignment must be -350 or
lower. Good/neutral NPCs and all players are ineligible.
It grants +1 hitroll, +1 damroll and +10 armor as one timed named blessing.
The armor stat rises, but current NPC avoidance uses level, not armor.
The offensive bonuses are the NPC combat buff. Repeated applications do
not stack; expiry/removal restores the old values.
The spell name is darkblessing; normal spell or item requirements apply.
~

0 CLASSBONUSES CLASSBENEFITS TRAININGBENEFITS~
CLASS BENEFITS | training, passives and activated powers

Class         Examples of real benefits
------------  ----------------------------------------------------------
Angel         Mastery traits; active wards, healing and support
Cyborg        Limbs/body combat bonuses; installed component traits
Deathknight   STR/CON/WIS mastery traits; deathbound powers
Demon         Mastery traits; active shapes, warps and powers
Dragon        Dragon-form rolls, armor, cap, soak and speed
Drow          Speed/roll/cap training; prayer and discipline unlocks
Elemental     Fire/Infinity cap; Earth soak; Wind/Time speed
Gargoyle      Visceratika armor, STR/CON and physical absorption
Highlander    Attack speed/roll/cap; Defense armor/soak
Kuei-jin      Track-based STR/CON/WIS; discipline unlocks
Mage          Mind cap; Time speed; sphere-based spell unlocks
Monk          Art combat bonuses; Tech/Mantra powers
Moogle        INT/WIS/DEX mastery traits; pom and support powers
Ninja         Ningenno speed; Chikyu cap; principle powers
Phoenix       Mastery unlocks paid flame powers, protection and flight
Sorcerer      Color-based native chanting; written spells and book tools
Vampire       Potence damage; Fortitude defense; active Celerity speed
Werewolf      Rank/tribe bonuses; breed and auspice powers
Wraith        Track-based DEX/WIS/CON; Arcanoi powers and utility

Training can unlock a power instead of adding a flat stat bonus.
Passives may start at a threshold. Active powers require activation,
resources, valid targets and normal prerequisites. Class pages explain them.
Bonuses are derived; passive restoration does not retrain base stats.
Normal integer rounding and combat caps still apply.

Werewolf corrections:
Skill         Benefit / restriction
------------  ----------------------------------------------------------
Philodox 3    +100 damage cap; reads auspice, not an unrelated tribe
Theurge 4     Order visible NPC spirits; never other players or another
              character's follower/familiar; named/all use the same gate

This table is not a promise that every individual legacy variant has been
certified. HELP KITSTATUS distinguishes implementation and tested coverage.
~

5 PSET PSETCURRENCIES STAFFCURRENCIES~
STAFF PSET | absolute player balances

Syntax: pset <player> currencies
        pset <player> <currency> <whole nonnegative amount>
Examples: pset Player classpoints 50000
          pset Player exp 5000000
          pset Player bionics 100000

Field             Meaning / common aliases
----------------  -------------------------------------------------------
exp               Experience; xp, experience
primal            Primal; primalpoints
gold              Gold; coins, money
classpoints       Spendable class points; cps, cp, dp, favor, favour
classpointstotal   Lifetime class-point field; cptotal, cp_total
questpoints       Quest points; quest, qp
mana / hit        Current mana or positive HP; hp, health
blood / willpower Current pool; will aliases willpower
ki / quintessence Ninja ki / Mage BODY quintessence; quint
nanites / bionics Cyborg resources; bionic
souls             Demon soul power; soulpower
energy            Moogle/Deathknight/Gargoyle/Kuei-jin/Wraith pool
humanity          Free Cyborg implant budget; freehumanity
humanitycap       Total Cyborg implant budget; humanitycapacity
bombs             Cyborg inventory; disarm before setting armed bombs to 0

Use currencies (or wallet) for exact current limits. Energy aliases are
pomenergy/pom, soulenergy, stoneenergy, chi and pathos, for their own class.
Positive nanites need an installed battery to survive login.
Humanity edits preserve installed spending; total budget may not exceed 1000.
Current and lifetime class points are independent. No mastery is granted.
Whole amounts only: no signs, fractions, overflow or trailing arguments.
Wrong-class or invalid-state edits fail without changes. This sets a balance,
not an addition. Training costs and existing stat/stance fields are unchanged.

Immortals only. NPCs and switched sessions are rejected. Another player of
equal/higher trust cannot be edited. Changes are logged and use normal
save/autosave rules; pset does not immediately force a disk save.
~

